vanessa i'm at centennial center off  tropical parkway in the northwest valley  this voting location was actually the  most popular early voting site in the  entire county  and it still seems to be today as people  are lining up this evening  to cast their ballot nearly 27 000  people voted here in october right now  all seems to be going well  voters are waiting about 10 to 15  minutes in line  some even less this afternoon but it may  be picking up as the work day  ends i spoke with a couple ages 71 and  66 were voting for the first time in  their life  they tell me it's an important enough  election to leave the house and cast  their ballot  the couple even commend the efficiency  of this site  it went really smooth you're in and out  in no time to vote so they'll help you  if you have any questions or anything  and it's great  there are 40 machines inside the tent  the election leader tells me  all have been working perfectly today  there was a slight  issue earlier metro had to be called out  and i'm told that's because people were  campaigning too close but that issue did  resolve itself so metro has  left the property now in order to cast a  ballot you must be in line at one of the  125 locations  in clark county by seven o'clock tonight  and you can also come here or  at any of those other locations to drop  off your mail ballot  reporting live in the northwest valley  kristen drummond 8 news now
 

